esolve names from stdin (found/ambiguous/missing)\r\n  files         Indexed file inventory with symbol/byte counts\r\n  search        Symbol-level search: bm25-ranked FTS5 over identifier tokens\r\n  clones        Duplicate-block candidates: normalized 5-line-window shingle matches\r\n  stats         Index totals: files, symbols, edges, parse errors, sizes\r\n  hotspots      Pain-ranking of files: cyclomatic + LOC + churn-90d + fix-density\r\n  report        Four-section architecture report (overview, map, hotspots, fan-in)\r\n  doctor        Inspect index health (integrity, versions, staleness, orphans)\r\n  usage         Summarize the usage journal: calls, errors, latency, empty/stale rates. --verify replays sampled payload pointers against current source\r\n  mcp           Run the MCP stdio server (newline-delimited JSON-RPC 2.0; Amendment 8)\r\n  help          Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)\r\n\r\nOptions:\r\n      --root \u003cROOT\u003e\r\n          Repository root (default: nearest git root ancestor of cwd). Global: valid before or after the subcommand\r\n\r\n      --no-journal\r\n          Disable the usage journal for this invocation (Amendment 6)\r\n\r\n  -h, --help\r\n          Print help (see a summary with '-h')\r\n\r\n  -V, --version\r\n          Print version\r\n"}}}
